1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
From the 2024.1 version, we have optimized the extension tool.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Now, in the case of the entire board left and right symmetrical and linked, the operation of the extension board is realized.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Now, through this video, let's learn in detail how to use the extension tool.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In the extension tool storage in the 2D tool bar, you can see that there are two extension tools here.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The extension board slice point and the extension board slice line.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Let's first look at the optimized extension tool.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Click on the extension board slice line.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The tool will switch to the extension board slice line.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You can see the icon and text prompt of the tool in the light bar.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Click on the starting and end points of section 1 that need to be extended.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Now we want to use the tool to extend the front and bottom.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
So, we use the extension as section 1.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Click on the starting and end points.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Complete the selection of section 1.

15
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The text prompt of the time icon has been changed.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Click on the starting and end points of section 2 that need to be extended.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The bottom line as section 2.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Select the starting and end points.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Complete the selection of section 2.

20
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Click on the extension board slice window.

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
You can enter the total length value of the bottom and section 2 according to the design requirements.

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
You can also enter the distance value that needs to be moved.

23
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
You can also enter the negative value to shorten the bottom.

24
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
All can be previewed in the 2D window.

25
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
After entering the value, click OK.

26
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The extension is completed in the front.

27
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Next, let's see how to use another extension tool, the extension board slice point.

28
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Extend the bottom of the back piece.

29
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Long press the extension board slice line.

30
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Click on the extension board slice point.

31
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The tool will switch to the extension board slice point.

32
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
You can see the icon and text prompt of the tool on the light bar.

33
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Click on the line and draw the baseline.

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Now we want to use the extension board slice bottom of the back piece of the tool.

35
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
You can use the side view point of the back piece as the starting point.

36
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The arrow pointing downwards appears.

37
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
You can press the Shift key.

38
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Draw a vertical baseline line according to the instruction line.

39
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
The extension position at the bottom as the end point.

40
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Click again.

41
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Complete the baseline line.

42
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
The light bar rotates clockwise to one side.

43
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The plate on this side of the baseline line will be extended with the side view point as the center.

44
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
You can also shorten the bottom.

45
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
There will be a text prompt on the light bar.

46
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Press the D key to maintain the frequency when rotating.

47
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
So we can press the D key when operating.

48
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Maintain the bottom frequency.

49
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
In the process of extension.

50
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The right click button will play the extension dialogue.

51
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
You can enter the length of the plate to be extended.

52
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Or enter the angle of the extension.

53
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
After entering, click OK.

54
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
So the back piece is completed.

55
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The above is the introduction of the extension tool.

56
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
I hope this function.

57
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Can make you more efficient in completing the plate extension.

